{"entryId":"1159","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1159:1","sourceSha256":"a4a7c5816d2c4ee71bc55f4033de9241ec2740ce28be69c7faebfc4a2f6647d9","englishSha256":"c94b6dba84da35a5e99403289e2af7c9eab695e894fa4b650e052e45576df6bf","citations":[{"id":"1159:1:citation-01","he":[238,253],"en":[369,382],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_71b.3"},"reference":"Kiddushin 71b:3","assessment":"Proposal, crossing and reply confirmed. Distinguish Heilprin’s lineage explanation from actual dialogue.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 71b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_71b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-02","he":[401,415],"en":[639,660],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_9b.18"},"reference":"Yoma 9b:18","assessment":"Rav Pappa presents alternatives, Resh Lakish with Zeiri or Rabbah bar bar Chana with Elazar.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 9b:17","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_9b.17"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 9b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_9b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-03","he":[584,602],"en":[911,922],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_54b.4"},"reference":"Chullin 54b:4","assessment":"Italian issar is Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel’s measure in the preceding mishnah. Zeiri on 54b gives the local Kordian dinar equivalent.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 54a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_54a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 54b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_54b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-04","he":[721,732],"en":[1120,1129],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_56a.6"},"reference":"Chullin 56a:6","assessment":"Original no examination and