 Batra 87a:10","assessment":"Elazar asks who Rav taught the laws of measures. Zeiri points to Yitzchak bar Avdimi; English him may mistakenly suggest Elazar.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 87a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_87a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-09","he":[1071,1087],"en":[1628,1640],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.2"},"reference":"Chullin 110a:2","assessment":"Elazar asks who taught Rav on udder. Yitzchak denies doing so in this digital witness. Preserve compiler’s tentative inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 110a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-10","he":[1203,1219],"en":[1802,1833],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_21a.2"},"reference":"Chullin 21a:2","assessment":"Bavli names Zira and Ammi. Bind antecedent Zeiri and Rashi’s exact gloss next.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 21a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_21a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-11","he":[1190,1201],"en":[1787,1801],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_21a.2.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 21a:2:1","assessment":"Rashi identifies Ammi’s ruling as Zeiri’s.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 21a:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_21a.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-12","he":[1240,1279],"en":[1866,1895],"target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_שני_אות_הה%22א"},"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin II, letter He","assessment":"Direct Yuchasin reports Zeiri as teacher and the unlocated Bavli attribution in his name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Yuchasin II, letter He","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/ספר_יוחסין_מאמר_שני_אות_הה%22א"},"witness":"Hebrew Wikisource, Sefer Yuchasin II, He"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-13","he":[1309,1330],"en":[1981,2025],"target":{"entry":1149,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1149:1","assessment":"Local pointer to the prior Zeira biography records Rav Huna transmitting Zeira, not independent confirmation of Yuchasin’s Zeiri reading.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1149:1","target":{"entry":1149,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-14","he":[1332,1353],"en":[2027,2064],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_77b.8"},"reference":"Yoma 77b:8","assessment":"Both versions of the travel account are consistent about teacher and student while reversing who visited whom. The pointed biography also names a Zeira form.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 77b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_77b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1228:1","target":{"entry":1228,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-15","he":[1365,1384],"en":[2096,2107],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17a.7"},"reference":"Shabbat 17a:7","assessment":"Each is Zeiri in Chanina’s name; 50a transmits it through Rav Dimi. Do not carry Chiyya bar Ashi as the speaker.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 17a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 17a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_17a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 50a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_50a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1159:1:citation-16","he":[1365,1384],"en":[2109,2112],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_50a.10"},"reference":"Shabbat 50a:10","assessment":"Each is Zeiri in Chanina’s name; 50a transmits it through Rav Di